  "notes": [
    "Baseline is PR head 4a10b7222d with identical benchmark fixture changes only. Final candidate matches the recorded source and immutable binary hashes.",
    "Alternating paired process execution with in-process warmup; setup excluded. Allocation-counting runs are separate from production-allocator timing. Each of three final document confirmations has 11 pairs at 10k documents; the separately identified intermediate candidate has ten fixtures.",
    "Requested backing-heap counters do not measure RSS or stack memory. This experiment does not establish equivalence or universal zero cost.",
    "Text descriptor reservation is restricted to batches of 16..256 containing entirely public document IDs, and counts visible store values. Mixed/internal batches and inline-only fallback rows retain lazy growth.",
    "Asset projection validates the key and decodes only its name. Plain names borrow input; escaped names use a bounded 256-byte stack fallback and the caller allocator for larger spills.",
    "Asset Boolean classification has identical ARM64 instruction count and opcode sequence to baseline; assembly comparison is binary-specific.",
    "A duplicate-map hot capacity guard reduced requested heap but slowed the duplicate-heavy microbenchmark by about 25%; rejected. Final normal getOrPut path is retained, with a duplicate check only following allocation failure and rollback following output-list failure. No steady-state allocation saving is claimed for this helper.",
    "A reservation prepass that parsed asset keys a second time slowed mixed documents/assets; rejected. A cheap namespace check with partial reservation still regressed mixed batches by about 16%; final reservation is disabled for any internal-key batch.",
    "The no-hint enrichment callback bypass is normally excluded by production scanners. Deferred scratch trimming is defensive cleanup, not evidence of a production memory leak.",
    "Vector preparation is unchanged in this round. Prior group-commit durable-retry uncertainty remains unresolved; universal zero runtime cost remains unproven.",
    "203 focused ReleaseSafe tests passed, with zero skipped/failed/leaked and 27/27 build steps. Boundary and storage-shard audits pass. Earlier full-text repair integration failure remains unresolved; the broad integration suite was not rerun.",
    "Final journal enrichment timing measured +0.82%, with bootstrap interval +0.32% to +1.95%; primary enrichment timing was inconclusive. Requested allocation counters were unchanged. This observed small slowdown is retained as a limitation."
  ],
